-## Binary And Multiclass Targets
-
-The default `scoring: "auto"` setting supports binary and multiclass labels:
-
-- SVM-L1 wrapper: binary uses `roc_auc`; multiclass uses `balanced_accuracy`
-  and aggregates class-wise coefficients by max absolute coefficient.
-- RFECV-RF: binary uses `roc_auc`; multiclass uses `roc_auc_ovr`.
-- XGBoost wrapper: binary uses `binary:logistic`; multiclass switches to
-  `multi:softprob`.
-- GA-RF: default `fitness_metric: "accuracy"` works for binary and multiclass.
-  Users may also set `fitness_metric: "balanced_accuracy"` or
-  `fitness_metric: "roc_auc_ovr"`.
-
