+## CLI overrides
 
-For the global RFECV best feature count:
+The main upgraded options are:
 
-```yaml
-rfecv:
-  method_max_features_to_consider:
-    xgboost:
-    svm_l1:
-    boruta_rf:
-```
+```text
+--ga-fitness-mode {legacy_zero_truncated_linear,untruncated_shifted_linear}
+--locking-strategy {top_k_jaccard_medoid,regret_constrained_medoid}
+--locking-tolerance-mode {absolute,relative,best_run_se_scaled,one_se}
+--regret-tolerance FLOAT
+--minimum-pool-size INT
+--unified-metric {accuracy,balanced_accuracy,roc_auc,macro_ovr_auroc}
+```
+
+For `regret_constrained_medoid`, selection is strictly restricted to candidates
+within the declared tolerance. The best-scoring candidate always has zero
+regret, so singleton eligible pools are valid and no score-based pool expansion
+is performed. `one_se` is retained only as a deprecated CLI/configuration alias
+for the more accurate name `best_run_se_scaled`; it is not the conventional
+paired one-standard-error model-selection rule.
+
+The recommended scientific tie path is mean eligible-pool Jaccard, higher
+locking score, smaller feature count, then the lexicographically smaller
+SHA-256 digest of the canonical `uint8` mask bytes. The hash provides stable
+ordering; it is not a scientific score. Candidate feature order is normalized
+against one common ordered candidate universe. Duplicate masks from distinct
+runs are retained as multiple voting candidates, so multiplicity is part of
+the supplied candidate bank. If exact duplicate records remain tied, they
+represent the same scientific feature set; the lowest source run ID is retained
+only as a provenance label after feature-set selection.
+
+Run `wrapevofs run --help` for the complete interface.
 
