+## Scope
 
-## Notes
+WrapEvoFS expects already extracted tabular features. It does not process raw imaging or assay files. Five-seed overlap is stochastic agreement on a fixed development set, not participant-resampling stability or biomarker validation.
 
-- This package expects already-extracted tabular features.
-- It does not process raw MRI images.
-- For reliable final validation, keep the held-out test set untouched until the
-  final model evaluation stage.
-- For small biomedical datasets, treat single-split test results carefully and
-  report stability across GA top solutions.
+The repository also contains an auxiliary GBM proteomics-to-ssGSEA benchmark. Its preserved Korean instructions are in [docs/GBM_BENCHMARK_KO.md](docs/GBM_BENCHMARK_KO.md); it is separate from the WrapEvoFS package API.
